# Database migrations (Alembic)

## Canonical layout

Use **only** this tree:

- Root config: `alembic.ini` (repo root)
- Scripts: `migrations/` (this directory)
- Revisions: `migrations/versions/`

```powershell
# From repo root
uv run python -m alembic upgrade head
# or
.\scripts\migrate_db.ps1
```

Do **not** create a second Alembic environment under `alembic/` or nested `migrations/alembic.ini`.
Those were removed as drift sources.

## One-off / legacy scripts

Historical data fixes live under `scripts/migrations_one_off/` and are **not** part of the
Alembic revision chain. Run them only when documented for a specific upgrade path.

## Fresh installs

The app lifespan still calls `Base.metadata.create_all()` as a safety net for local
bootstrapping. Prefer `alembic upgrade head` so revision history stays authoritative.
